1:1 COMMENT "# cli_driver.z -- what a program with commands needs from cli. The command is"
1:78 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# position 1, so reading starts at 2 (`first:`). `--src` repeats: `optionAll`"
2:78 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# answers every value in the order written, and `option` the last. `given` says"
3:80 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# whether a name was written at all. With `stopAtOperand` the first operand"
4:76 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# past the declared positionals ends the reading: it and every token after it"
5:78 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# are extra arguments, read or not, as the arguments of a program that `run`"
6:77 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# starts. `errorText` is the sentence for an error."
7:52 EOL "\n"
8:1 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# valueText -- an accessor's answer: the value in brackets, or `none`"
9:70 EOL "\n"
